<body>
<w t="0" id="1" wp="1" ws="1"/>
<p t="160" d="7240" w="1"><s ac="0">Please welcome to the stage the Attorney
General of the United States, Todd</s></p>
<p t="4400" d="3000" w="1"><s ac="0">Blanch.</s></p>
<p t="10480" d="2020" w="1">[music]</p>
<p t="15839" d="3241" w="1"><s ac="0">Thank you.</s></p>
<p t="19119" d="6801" w="1"><s ac="0">Thank you. Good afternoon.
Welcome to the Department of Justice.</s></p>
<p t="23199" d="7041" w="1"><s ac="0">And I want to be the first to welcome uh
President Trump to his second trip back</s></p>
<p t="28240" d="6560" w="1"><s ac="0">to the Department of Justice as a 47th
President of the United States. We are</s></p>
<p t="32079" d="7121" w="1"><s ac="0">honored, humbled, and thrilled to have
you join us today, Mr. President. And on</s></p>
<p t="37040" d="7359" w="1"><s ac="0">behalf of the prosecutors in the room,
the law enforcement members in the room,</s></p>
<p t="41440" d="7520" w="1"><s ac="0">and everybody that&#39;s here today, let me
just tell you that we are here. We are</s></p>
<p t="46399" d="6961" w="1"><s ac="0">so appreciative that President Trump
delivered on his promise to the American</s></p>
<p t="50800" d="7200" w="1"><s ac="0">people that when he took office again
that he would do everything in his power</s></p>
<p t="55120" d="8079" w="1"><s ac="0">to unleash law enforcement to do their
jobs to keep this country safe again,</s></p>
<p t="61520" d="7720" w="1"><s ac="0">which is exactly what he&#39;s done. So,
thank you, Mr. President. We&#39;re also on</s></p>
<p t="65920" d="3320" w="1"><s ac="0">Thank you.</s></p>
<p t="69280" d="7839" w="1"><s ac="0">We&#39;re also honored to welcome some of
the families of the victims whose lives</s></p>
<p t="75200" d="8320" w="1"><s ac="0">were forever changed by the vicious
behavior of the death row inmates whose</s></p>
<p t="80880" d="8160" w="1"><s ac="0">sentences have now been commuted by
Governor Nuome. Thank you very much for</s></p>
<p t="86240" d="9839" w="1"><s ac="0">being here today and thank you for
speaking up. Mr. President, on day one,</s></p>
<p t="93840" d="6560" w="1"><s ac="0">on day one of your presidency, you
issued an executive order that directed</s></p>
<p t="98240" d="8400" w="1"><s ac="0">the Department of Justice to seek the
death penalty wherever appropriate.</s></p>
<p t="103840" d="9440" w="1"><s ac="0">Since January 20th of last year, the
Department of Justice has done so 49</s></p>
<p t="109920" d="7760" w="1"><s ac="0">times. Now, when you compare that to the
last administration, during the last</s></p>
<p t="115520" d="6559" w="1"><s ac="0">administration, the Department of
Justice sought the death penalty one</s></p>
<p t="120240" d="7440" w="1"><s ac="0">time.
One time. That is not justice. That is</s></p>
<p t="125600" d="6639" w="1"><s ac="0">not what the American people deserve.
That is not what the families of victims</s></p>
<p t="129599" d="6000" w="1"><s ac="0">of horrific murders deserve. And so, Mr.
President, I assure you that this</s></p>
<p t="134080" d="7200" w="1"><s ac="0">Department of Justice is seeking the
death penalty whenever appropriate for</s></p>
<p t="138400" d="7839" w="1"><s ac="0">crimes get committed in this country.
So,</s></p>
<p t="143520" d="7200" w="1"><s ac="0">I want to take just a moment
and tell every law enforcement member</s></p>
<p t="148160" d="6719" w="1"><s ac="0">watching or here in this room that we
have your back, that President Trump has</s></p>
<p t="152879" d="7521" w="1"><s ac="0">your back, and he will always have your
back. to the families</s></p>
<p t="158640" d="6640" w="1"><s ac="0">to the families of the victims of the
horrible crimes that have been committed</s></p>
<p t="163440" d="7120" w="1"><s ac="0">not only in California but around this
country. Make no mistake about it that</s></p>
<p t="168080" d="7519" w="1"><s ac="0">this Department of Justice every single
day that our prosecutors that our</s></p>
<p t="172480" d="8880" w="1"><s ac="0">federal agents will do everything we can
to impose the harshest penalty possible</s></p>
<p t="178800" d="6560" w="1"><s ac="0">under the facts of the case consistent
with the president&#39;s agenda. That&#39;s what</s></p>
<p t="183200" d="9039" w="1"><s ac="0">we have done since January 20th. of what
we will continue to do from this day</s></p>
<p t="187840" d="10560" w="1"><s ac="0">going forward. So with that, let me be
um let me just ask everybody to get on</s></p>
<p t="194640" d="8412" w="1"><s ac="0">their feet and welcome the 45th and 47th
president of the United States,</s></p>
<p t="200080" d="4992" w="1"><s ac="0">President Donald J. Trump.
[music]</s></p>
<p t="211567" d="2020" w="1">&gt;&gt; [music]</p>
<p t="219440" d="3079" w="1"><s ac="0">&gt;&gt; Heat. Heat.</s></p>
<p t="231872" d="2020" w="1">&gt;&gt; [music]</p>
<p t="237112" d="2020" w="1">[music]</p>
<p t="241697" d="2020" w="1">[music]</p>
<p t="246319" d="10320" w="1"><s ac="0">&gt;&gt; Thank you very much. Please. Thank you.
It&#39;s a great honor.</s></p>
<p t="252640" d="10559" w="1"><s ac="0">I want to just welcome all of you to a
very safe Washington DC. You know, the</s></p>
<p t="260320" d="7520" w="1"><s ac="0">crime rates gone down 84%
and a lot of the people in this room are</s></p>
<p t="264960" d="8480" w="1"><s ac="0">responsible for that. And I want to
thank you to a very special thanks to an</s></p>
<p t="271520" d="4880" w="1"><s ac="0">outstanding attorney general. It&#39;s going
to be one of the greats. I think he&#39;ll</s></p>
<p t="274880" d="6840" w="1"><s ac="0">go down as one of the greats when we&#39;re
finished. Todd Blanch. Thank you, Todd.</s></p>
<p t="278320" d="3400" w="1"><s ac="0">Appreciate it.</s></p>
<p t="283840" d="8000" w="1"><s ac="0">Where is he? What happened? He&#39;s around.
He&#39;s around here someplace. I can&#39;t I</s></p>
<p t="289520" d="7600" w="1"><s ac="0">want to say hello to Todd. He&#39;s special.
He works all the time. We&#39;re here today</s></p>
<p t="295040" d="6879" w="1"><s ac="0">to talk about one of the most shocking
acts of injustice our country has ever</s></p>
<p t="300240" d="5840" w="1"><s ac="0">seen. I couldn&#39;t believe it. I witnessed
it a couple of weeks ago. I couldn&#39;t</s></p>
<p t="303600" d="9200" w="1"><s ac="0">believe it. Just days ago, the governor
of California, Gavin Nuome, granted</s></p>
<p t="309199" d="10321" w="1"><s ac="0">clemency and mercy to 548 of the most
evil monsters on the face of the earth.</s></p>
<p t="316479" d="6961" w="1"><s ac="0">You&#39;d have to read their biographies to
see how bad they were. Some of them you</s></p>
<p t="322080" d="8480" w="1"><s ac="0">wouldn&#39;t even believe it. All of them,
but some of them you would levels of</s></p>
<p t="327360" d="7760" w="1"><s ac="0">craziness, sickness that I&#39;ve never seen
before.</s></p>
<p t="332080" d="9200" w="1"><s ac="0">Among those death row inmates he granted
clemency were more than 110 child</s></p>
<p t="338800" d="6640" w="1"><s ac="0">killers, more than 100 rapists who
murdered their victims, and numerous</s></p>
<p t="343759" d="6641" w="1"><s ac="0">serial killers who tortured and
slaughtered dozens of innocent people</s></p>
<p t="348560" d="7199" w="1"><s ac="0">at levels that nobody&#39;s ever seen
before.</s></p>
<p t="352000" d="9039" w="1"><s ac="0">Among the serial killers he spared is
Charles Ing, who tortured, enslaved, and</s></p>
<p t="358800" d="8160" w="1"><s ac="0">slaughtered at least 11 people,
including babies, in a torture chamber</s></p>
<p t="363600" d="10080" w="1"><s ac="0">in a remote cabin, as well as the
Southside Slayer who killed 14 women and</s></p>
<p t="370319" d="9121" w="1"><s ac="0">enjoyed every moment of it in an unborn
child in South Los Angeles.</s></p>
<p t="377280" d="8800" w="1"><s ac="0">and the scorecard killer. They call him
the scorecard killer who kept a tally in</s></p>
<p t="383600" d="8159" w="1"><s ac="0">his car of at least 16 young men he
abducted, raped and murdered. And the</s></p>
<p t="389039" d="8481" w="1"><s ac="0">alphabet killer was that name, alphabet
killer, who raped and murdered innocent</s></p>
<p t="394560" d="9199" w="1"><s ac="0">young girls whose first and last name
started with the same letter. He needed</s></p>
<p t="400240" d="8560" w="1"><s ac="0">that same letter. These are sick people.
This afternoon, we come together to</s></p>
<p t="405759" d="7681" w="1"><s ac="0">stand against the travesty and to wrap
our arms around the families of victims</s></p>
<p t="410880" d="8640" w="1"><s ac="0">who were so cruy betrayed by bad
government and our political system. To</s></p>
<p t="417199" d="9681" w="1"><s ac="0">every parent, son, daughter, sibling, or
spouse here today whose loved one was</s></p>
<p t="422880" d="10640" w="1"><s ac="0">brutally killed by those monsters, we
love you. We support you and we are with</s></p>
<p t="429440" d="8879" w="1"><s ac="0">you and your quest for un really the the
ultimate of final justice. We have to do</s></p>
<p t="436319" d="7921" w="1"><s ac="0">this. We can&#39;t let this happen. What
happened to you, what happened to all of</s></p>
<p t="440000" d="10319" w="1"><s ac="0">us should not be allowed to stand. What
these families have endured is beyond</s></p>
<p t="447440" d="8159" w="1"><s ac="0">imagination.
One day their lives were shattered into</s></p>
<p t="453199" d="6720" w="1"><s ac="0">pieces when they learned that someone
they had loved most in the entire world</s></p>
<p t="458080" d="7760" w="1"><s ac="0">they loved more than anybody in the
world had spent their final moments in</s></p>
<p t="463039" d="10081" w="1"><s ac="0">excruciating pain and bone chilling
terror and those families lives will</s></p>
<p t="470000" d="7840" w="1"><s ac="0">never ever be the same. Then after the
juries delivered their verdicts and the</s></p>
<p t="475520" d="6880" w="1"><s ac="0">justice system returned a muchdeserved
sentence of death,</s></p>
<p t="480560" d="6880" w="1"><s ac="0">Nuome,
a terrible governor in so many other</s></p>
<p t="484400" d="7760" w="1"><s ac="0">ways, came along and stole away the only
closure those families</s></p>
<p t="490080" d="7280" w="1"><s ac="0">might ever have.
He stood with the murderers and the</s></p>
<p t="494319" d="7361" w="1"><s ac="0">child slayers. But today, we say, the
American people, stand with you. We</s></p>
<p t="500240" d="9760" w="1"><s ac="0">stand with you. We&#39;re not going to let
this happen.</s></p>
<p t="504960" d="11439" w="1"><s ac="0">In May 1996, 8-year-old Michael Lions
was walking home from elementary school</s></p>
<p t="513360" d="10080" w="1"><s ac="0">in Yuba City, California,
when he was abducted by convicted sex</s></p>
<p t="519519" d="10440" w="1"><s ac="0">offender Robert Boyd Rhodess, who forced
young Michael into a secluded area,</s></p>
<p t="525760" d="4199" w="1"><s ac="0">raped and tortured him</s></p>
<p t="530320" d="8800" w="1"><s ac="0">for extended periods of time. The
predators slashed Michael more than a</s></p>
<p t="535519" d="10320" w="1"><s ac="0">hundred times with a knife and left his
body on a river bank for others to pick</s></p>
<p t="542080" d="8960" w="1"><s ac="0">up. Roads was captured and sentenced to
death. But Gavin Newsome thought that</s></p>
<p t="548640" d="7680" w="1"><s ac="0">child killer was owed the mercy that he
never showed to 8-year-old</s></p>
<p t="553920" d="8080" w="1"><s ac="0">Michael. We&#39;re joined by Michael&#39;s
family, including his mother, Sandy. And</s></p>
<p t="559200" d="6199" w="1"><s ac="0">Sandy, I&#39;d like to have you say a few
words, please.</s></p>
<p t="566560" d="5480" w="1"><s ac="0">&gt;&gt; Thank you.
Thank you, darling.</s></p>
<p t="572240" d="8960" w="1"><s ac="0">Hi, my name is Sandy Friend. I am the
mother of Michael Lions.</s></p>
<p t="578560" d="10399" w="1"><s ac="0">Michael was eight years old. He loved
his sisters, fishing ninja turtles,</s></p>
<p t="586000" d="9360" w="1"><s ac="0">telling campfire stories,
and bringing me flowers.</s></p>
<p t="592240" d="6880" w="1"><s ac="0">Michael was afraid of the dark. He
believed the boogeyman was going to get</s></p>
<p t="597440" d="8959" w="1"><s ac="0">him.
On May 16th, 1996, Robert Boyd Rhodess,</s></p>
<p t="603440" d="9200" w="1"><s ac="0">a twice convicted sex offender and
serial killer, kidnapped Michael.</s></p>
<p t="609839" d="10240" w="1"><s ac="0">Walking home from school, he took my
little boy into the darkness. His most</s></p>
<p t="616399" d="8601" w="1"><s ac="0">feared thing was the dark. That night,
Michael learned that the boogeyman was</s></p>
<p t="622000" d="3000" w="1"><s ac="0">real.</s></p>
<p t="626880" d="11120" w="1"><s ac="0">Mikey was raped, sodomized, and tortured
from 10 for 10 hours. From the very</s></p>
<p t="634720" d="8840" w="1"><s ac="0">first inflicted stabin
to the last,</s></p>
<p t="640240" d="3320" w="1"><s ac="0">he only</s></p>
<p t="646640" d="7600" w="1"><s ac="0">that is why the killer was convicted of
torture.</s></p>
<p t="651200" d="12322" w="1"><s ac="0">A jury sentenced him to die and in
December 2025 a judge reaffirmed that</s></p>
<p t="658160" d="10160" w="1"><s ac="0">sentence. The go the governor then sorry
[sighs]</s></p>
<p t="664560" d="9440" w="1"><s ac="0">this is so very hard. [gasps]
Then Governor Nome erased that with the</s></p>
<p t="671519" d="6921" w="1"><s ac="0">swipe of a pen
without notifying the families.</s></p>
<p t="678800" d="10400" w="1"><s ac="0">Governor Nuome,
we deserve to be heard.</s></p>
<p t="685040" d="9919" w="1"><s ac="0">You never heard what my child endured or
lived with the emptiness of having an</s></p>
<p t="692000" d="8000" w="1"><s ac="0">empty chair at every holiday and
milestone.</s></p>
<p t="696480" d="8720" w="1"><s ac="0">Yet you took the only justice we had and
left families feeling abandoned by the</s></p>
<p t="702399" d="8081" w="1"><s ac="0">state that promised to protect us.
You&#39;ll never understand the unimaginable</s></p>
<p t="708079" d="8561" w="1"><s ac="0">pain that you&#39;re putting these families
through. Face me, Governor Nuome. Tell</s></p>
<p t="714640" d="8319" w="1"><s ac="0">me, Michael&#39;s
Michael&#39;s life doesn&#39;t matter.</s></p>
<p t="720399" d="8000" w="1"><s ac="0">Michael deserved a governor who who
would stand with the victims, honor</s></p>
<p t="725600" d="8400" w="1"><s ac="0">their justice, and respect the will of
the people. You may have taken our</s></p>
<p t="731279" d="7761" w="1"><s ac="0">justice, but we will never you will
never take Michael&#39;s voice.</s></p>
<p t="736880" d="8720" w="1"><s ac="0">Mr. President, thank you for standing
with the victims and giving us a voice.</s></p>
<p t="742560" d="11920" w="1"><s ac="0">I will never stop speaking Michael&#39;s
name. Every victim matters. Look at his</s></p>
<p t="750000" d="7720" w="1"><s ac="0">face. He was only eight years old.
Thank you.</s></p>
<p t="776320" d="7840" w="1"><s ac="0">Sandy, we will always be with you. And
you&#39;re beautiful, Michael. And thank you</s></p>
<p t="781680" d="7920" w="1"><s ac="0">very much. It&#39;s great bravery even to be
here because Todd and the whole group, a</s></p>
<p t="786800" d="8080" w="1"><s ac="0">lot of people in this room are working
as hard as they can to get this travesty</s></p>
<p t="791839" d="10081" w="1"><s ac="0">overturned in some form. Very unusual
situation. state. We&#39;re we&#39;re very</s></p>
<p t="798560" d="11519" w="1"><s ac="0">active doing everything we can. In
October 1993, 12-year-old Polyclass was</s></p>
<p t="806399" d="10240" w="1"><s ac="0">having a slumber party at her home in
Paluma, California, when a violent</s></p>
<p t="812800" d="12159" w="1"><s ac="0">repeat offender out of parole slipped
into her home carrying a large violent</s></p>
<p t="821680" d="8480" w="1"><s ac="0">knife. He bound and gagged Pauliey&#39;s two
